          %p
            When looking at fibrations over a fixed base
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0=G_0=1_{\mathcal{B}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_0
            is the identity natural transformation. In that case,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            reduces to a natural transformation between the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1
            whose components are vertical, i.e. stay in the fibers.
